From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 21:51:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 39/49] fix(github-pr-review): gate run-review on its review
 workflow's outcome (gcp-m7dn)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

run-review launched the generic code-review formula with `gc sling ...
--formula` and then never consulted the run it started. Its only success
criterion was "REPORT_PATH exists and validates through github_reports.py
review-outcome" — satisfied by ANY conformant file on disk, including one
hand-authored to bridge a review that had already failed. A review workflow
that closed FAIL therefore walked the adapter to a pass and a verdict got
posted to GitHub anyway.

Worse, the criterion was unsatisfiable on the failure path: when the child dies
the report is never written, so the step had no legal exit at all. Two live
runs hit it and resolved it opposite ways — th-9fd3 hand-authored a bridging
verdict-report.md and closed PASS, th-kjcf closed fail and filed a bug. Whether
this pipeline fails closed depended on how an LLM step chose to read an
impossible instruction.

graph.v2 already computes the answer this step needs. When a workflow's
`workflow-finalize` runs, the orchestrator aggregates its steps into one
pass/fail and closes the workflow ROOT with that outcome (formula-spec-v2
section 3.5). This commit reads that engine-computed verdict instead of
inferring one:

- New `assets/scripts/workflow_outcome.py`. `root-outcome` resolves one
  launched workflow's terminal outcome from `gc bd`, failing closed on an
  unreadable, still-open, or unstamped root, and cross-checking members for a
  terminal `gc.outcome=fail`. It mirrors the engine's retry firewall
  (internal/dispatch/runtime.go:terminalAbortScopeFailure) by exempting
  superseded `gc.attempt` beads and transient failure classes, so a retried
  attempt cannot outvote the logical step that later passed. `review-gate`
  composes that with verdict-report validation for this adapter.
- run-review now slings with `--json`, records the child root id as
  `gc.github.review_workflow_id` (so a retried step resumes the launch rather
  than slinging a second review), polls the gate, and closes pass only when the
  child terminated pass AND the report validates. A non-pass child closes the
  step `gc.outcome=fail` / `gc.failure_class=hard` with
  `gc.github.review_child_outcome` recorded.

The gate deliberately keeps two things apart: a review report whose own verdict
is `fail/minor|major|blocker` is a review FINDING, not a workflow failure — it
still passes the gate and maps to comment/request_changes/block, matching the
role contract that findings are output rather than execution failure. Only "the
review did not run" stops the adapter. The step text also now names the
route-around explicitly and forbids it, because prose that merely omits an
option is what th-9fd3 filled in on its own.

Validation: 20 new unit tests in gascity/tests/test_workflow_outcome.py cover
the red case (child closed fail, valid report present -> gate refuses) and the
green control (child closed pass -> gate approves; findings-bearing report
still approves), plus incomplete/unknown/missing-root/retry-attempt/transient
paths. A new contract test in test_formula_assets.py pins the step text to the
gate. `gc lint gascity` is clean.

Not covered here: propagating a failed run-review so render-comment and
post-comment do not run. That is the abort_scope half, wired today only as a
city-local whole-file fork of the formula; the next commit folds it upstream.

Pre-existing and untouched: tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py and three
test_city_claim_command_* subtests fail identically on a clean checkout.
